-- title:
--   Invariance of the in-line polynomial under P↦[a]P
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a field with decidable equality, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $T$, and $\ell$ a prime with $\ell\neq 2$ whose image in $T$ is nonzero; assume $\Delta(W)\neq 0$, so that $W$ is elliptic. Let $x,y\in T$ satisfy the affine Weierstrass equation of $W$ and suppose that the division polynomial $W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{\ell}$ vanishes at $x$. Let $a\in\mathbb{Z}$ with $\ell\nmid a$, and let $x',y'\in T$ also satisfy the affine Weierstrass equation, subject to the relation that the point attached to $(x',y')$ equals $a$ times the point attached to $(x,y)$ in the group of affine points of the base change of $W$ to $T$; here the point attached to a pair is [`ModularCurve.LevelRelabelling.toPoint`](def/ModularCurve_LevelRelabelling.html#L22), namely `Point.some` of the pair if it is a nonsingular point and the point at infinity otherwise. Then for every natural number $n$ there is a nonzero $u\in T$ with
--   $$\prod_{b=1}^{(\ell-1)/2}\bigl(\Phi_n\cdot(\Psi^2_b)(x')-(\Phi_b)(x')\cdot\Psi^2_n\bigr)=u\cdot\prod_{b=1}^{(\ell-1)/2}\bigl(\Phi_n\cdot(\Psi^2_b)(x)-(\Phi_b)(x)\cdot\Psi^2_n\bigr)$$
--   in $T[X]$, i.e. `inLineMulPoly W ℓ n x'` is the constant $u$ times `inLineMulPoly W ℓ n x`.
--
--   The polynomial `inLineMulPoly W ℓ n x₀` cuts out the abscissae of those points $G$ for which $[n]G$ lies in the cyclic subgroup generated by the $\ell$-torsion point with abscissa $x₀$, minus the origin; the statement records that this subgroup, and hence the polynomial up to a unit, is unchanged when the generator $P$ is replaced by $[a]P$ with $\ell\nmid a$, which is the invariance of the level structure under the diamond scalars. It is used in the construction of fibre dictionaries for the $\Gamma_1(\ell^{\bullet})$ rigid data on the full-level modular curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_inLineMulPoly_eq_C_mul_of_toPoint_eq_zsmul_of_eval_prePsi_eq_zero.lean

